# The typed branch of a program that uses the binary naturals'
# constructors and operations: one lemma says that a context C applied to
# the eight names binary_zero, binary_even, binary_odd, merge_binary_plus,
# binary_maximum, binary_minimum, binary_bitwise_or and fixpoint equals the
# choice of itself and the marker wren_typed_branch applied to C applied to
# their typed versions, the defines of the directory wren_typed_block/: for
# the seven binary names wren_typed_Name, each Name under the arrow contract
# of native_types at the filters binary_set true and binary_set false, which
# binary_prolog_backend specializes natively; for fixpoint
# wren_fixpoint_by_value, Turing's combinator with its self-application
# under a λ, equal to fixpoint by η, the form a strict reading ends on. A
# program T holding all eight names matches the left side by the n-ary
# reverse beta of the framework's saturator (`ReverseBeta`, run by
# `HigherOrderSaturator` on the inputs' spelling), C being T with
# the names abstracted, so T gets one choice whose marked member is T with
# every occurrence of the eight replaced by its typed version: the choice
# outermost, and inside the marked member every type fact a filter
# `x ∥ binary_set p` of a typed version.
#
# The marker is β-equal to the identity; it says, in the term, which member
# of the choice is the typed branch, so a reader may read that member first
# and fall back to the other when it gives no normal form. Its body is not
# the identity's, so that no other identity shares its handle.
#
# The marker and the typed versions are noinline, so that the e-graph reads
# each as a leaf and the lemma never matches inside its own right side: the
# typed member holds none of the eight names outside those leaves.
#
# The lemma is a theorem of λ-lattice-η, by the paper proof
# wren_typed_branch_in_context: each Name ⊑ its typed version, application is monotone in each
# argument, so C applied to the names ⊑ C applied to the typed versions, and
# the marker is the identity by β. Dropping the untyped member loses answers
# only, never adds one (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Terms", specialization).
#
# Termination of this module's saturation, derived and not proved: the
# lemma's left side is a class applied to the eight names in order. Such
# nodes are the reverse beta redexes made over the inputs' spelling, one per
# subterm of an input that holds all eight names, which is a set fixed by
# the input, plus any already written in the input. The right side holds the
# marker and the typed versions, noinline leaves, and none of the eight names
# outside C, so an instance makes no new match. The instances are at most
# those nodes.
